  "pride_metadata": {
    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD046654",
      "title": "Sustainability of specific improvements of cardiorespiratory fitness and insulin sensitive metabolism in type 2 diabetes after exercise training",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "High intensity interval training (HIIT) improves metabolism, but maybe with differences in sustainability between prediabetes and type 2 diabetes (T2D). We hypothesized that HIIT-induced changes are maintained after 4-week detraining in humans with (20 T2D) and without T2D (12 insulin-sensitive, IS-NDM; 10 insulin-resistant, IR-NDM). To explore the change in protein cargo of small extracellular vesicles (SEV), we measured the proteome of SEVs from serum of T2D, IR-NMD and IR-NDM individuals.",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "All volunteers meeting the inclusion criteria, underwent comprehensive screening before entering the 12-week supervised cycle ergometer  training protocol. All individuals participated in the subsequent 4-week detraining study. In aliquots of 0.5 ml serum, SEV were isolated  by size exclusion chromatography (SEC), using the columns (qEV2/70 nm) from Izon Science (Addington, New Zealand) coupled to successive ultracentrifugation (17). A total of 200 \u00b5l of PBS-eluted SEV were centrifuged at 100,000 g for 70 min for mass spectrometry (MS) analysis. Extracellular vesicles were prepared and measured by MS using an Orbitrap Exploris 480 system (ThermoFisher Scientific).",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "For analysis, Pulsar search (Spectronaut Pulsar, Version 15, Biognosys, Schlieren, Switzerland) of data independent analysis (DIA) data was performed against a human FASTA file (UniProt reference proteome, Homo sapiens TaxID 9096, proteome UP000005640, version 06-2021). Results were filtered by a false discovery rate (FDR) of 1% on precursor and protein group level (q-value <0.01). For quantitative analysis the data-independent acquisition (DIA) data were analyzed in Spectronaut (Version 15, Biognosys, Schlieren, Switzerland) using an in-house sample specific library (17) supplemented by DIA runs with default  settings.",
      "projectTags": [],
      "keywords": [
        "Exercise; detraining; insulin sensitivity; mitochondrial function; small extracellular vesicles; inter-organ crosstalk"
      ],
